Categories: transitive-include and extension.
1. The lexer (and the amalgamated header, and the copy of v3.10.5 the ABI tests use) uses errno
and ERANGE without including <cerrno>; adds it. The vendored doctest likewise.
2. unit-regression2.cpp's test of parsing a span of std::byte instantiates
std::char_traits<std::byte>, which the standard does not define ([char.traits.specializations]):
libstdc++'s generic char_traits is an extension; json already excludes the test with libc++. Runs
it only with libstdc++ (__GLIBCXX__).

diff --git a/include/nlohmann/detail/input/lexer.hpp b/include/nlohmann/detail/input/lexer.hpp
